WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:15.927
At last Dorothy and her friends exited the forest.

2
00:00:15.928 --> 00:00:20.639
In front of them lay open land—and a river with a powerful current.

3
00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.852
The Tin Man eyed the river.

4
00:00:22.853 --> 00:00:26.456
"How will we cross that river?" he asked his friends.

5
00:00:26.457 --> 00:00:29.507
"Oh, that's easy," said the Scarecrow.

6
00:00:29.508 --> 00:00:34.345
"You will cut some logs, and we will build a raft."

7
00:00:34.346 --> 00:00:42.190
With the Tin Man's ax, the Lion's strength, and the Scarecrow's encouragement, a raft was soon built.

8
00:00:42.191 --> 00:00:45.366
"How will we steer the raft?" asked Dorothy.

9
00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:49.099
"We'll make long poles," replied the Scarecrow.

10
00:00:49.100 --> 00:01:01.123
"We will push the raft across the river."

11
00:01:01.124 --> 00:01:04.408
"Careful!" shouted the Tin Man to the Lion.

12
00:01:04.409 --> 00:01:07.729
"If I fall into the river, I'll rust for sure."

13
00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:10.981
"Sorry," said the Lion.

14
00:01:10.982 --> 00:01:16.047
"Use the poles to push us off," said the Scarecrow.

15
00:01:16.048 --> 00:01:21.667
They all pushed hard and were soon making their way across the river.

16
00:01:21.668 --> 00:01:26.773
The Tin Man looked nervous. "This isn't good," he said.

17
00:01:26.774 --> 00:01:30.976
"No, not at all," said the Scarecrow.

18
00:01:30.977 --> 00:01:34.318
"What's wrong?" asked Dorothy.

19
00:01:34.319 --> 00:01:40.927
"If the river takes us any farther downriver," answered the Tin Man, "we'll be in trouble."

20
00:01:40.928 --> 00:01:45.954
"Yes," said the Lion, who was starting to cry.

21
00:01:45.955 --> 00:01:52.618
"It'll take us to the Wicked Witch of the West. She'll kill us for sure!"

22
00:01:52.619 --> 00:02:04.644
"Oh no!" exclaimed Dorothy.

23
00:02:04.645 --> 00:02:07.977
"Help!" cried the Scarecrow suddenly.

24
00:02:07.978 --> 00:02:12.399
Everyone looked and realized the Scarecrow was no longer on the raft.

25
00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:16.140
He was holding onto his pole in the middle of the river.

26
00:02:16.141 --> 00:02:19.541
"What should we do?" shouted Dorothy.

27
00:02:19.542 --> 00:02:25.631
"Good-bye!" shouted the Scarecrow, waving from the pole.

28
00:02:25.632 --> 00:02:28.535
The Tin Man began to cry.

29
00:02:28.536 --> 00:02:31.040
"Stop," said Dorothy.

30
00:02:31.041 --> 00:02:36.172
"Crying will make you rust, and that will make a bad situation worse."

31
00:02:36.173 --> 00:02:39.652
The Tin Man dried his eyes on Dorothy's dress.

32
00:02:39.653 --> 00:02:44.799
"We must get across, or we are doomed," said the Lion.

33
00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:56.602
"I can swim, but you must hold my tail and pull the raft."

34
00:02:56.603 --> 00:03:00.808
"What should we do now?" said the Tin Man when they had reached shore.

35
00:03:00.809 --> 00:03:04.573
"We must get back to the road," said Dorothy.

36
00:03:04.574 --> 00:03:10.542
"We should follow the river upstream," said the Lion, shaking himself dry.

37
00:03:10.543 --> 00:03:22.293
"It will take us back to the road."

38
00:03:22.294 --> 00:03:28.068
"Look," said the Tin Man, pointing to the Scarecrow perched upon his pole.

39
00:03:28.069 --> 00:03:31.579
"How can we save him?" asked Dorothy.

40
00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:37.532
"Well, if one of you could fly, it would be easy," said the Scarecrow.

41
00:03:37.533 --> 00:03:41.682
Just then a great white stork flew overhead.

42
00:03:41.683 --> 00:03:46.577
"Mr. Stork!" shouted the Tin Man.

43
00:03:46.578 --> 00:03:50.372
"It's Mrs. Stork," said the Stork, annoyed.

44
00:03:50.373 --> 00:03:54.354
"Oh, don't listen to the Tin Man," said Dorothy sweetly.

45
00:03:54.355 --> 00:03:58.009
"I can see you are a wonderful mother."

46
00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:05.238
"Why yes, I am," said the Stork happily. "And who are you?"

47
00:04:05.239 --> 00:04:08.202
"I'm Dorothy and these are my friends.

48
00:04:08.203 --> 00:04:13.504
We are on our way to see the Wizard of Oz," she said.

49
00:04:13.505 --> 00:04:19.726
"I see," said the Stork, "but this isn't the road to Oz."

50
00:04:19.727 --> 00:04:26.180
"I know," said Dorothy. "Our friend needs our help, but none of us can fly."

51
00:04:26.181 --> 00:04:30.260
"I can fly," said the Stork proudly.

52
00:04:30.261 --> 00:04:33.872
"Could you help our friend?" asked Dorothy.

53
00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:38.716
"He looks heavy," said the Stork.

54
00:04:38.717 --> 00:04:44.395
"Oh no, he's very light," replied Dorothy. "He's made of straw."

55
00:04:44.396 --> 00:04:50.678
The Stork flew to the Scarecrow, grabbed him with her claws, and easily brought him to shore.

56
00:04:50.679 --> 00:04:55.806
"Thank you," said the Scarecrow, happy to be back with his friends.

57
00:04:55.807 --> 00:05:02.018
"That's all right," said the Stork. "I like to help people who are in trouble.

58
00:05:02.019 --> 00:05:07.389
Now I must return to my babies. Have a good trip to Oz."

59
00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:11.546
Dorothy and her friends waved good-bye as the Stork flew away.

60
00:05:11.547 --> 00:05:18.431
"Look!" shouted the Lion. "There's the Yellow Brick Road."

61
00:05:18.432 --> 00:05:22.104
"Let's get back to the road," said Dorothy happily.

62
00:05:22.105 --> 00:05:25.460
She started to run, and her friends followed her.

63
00:05:25.461 --> 00:05:32.381
Soon Dorothy stumbled because she felt sleepy. But she did not get up.

64
00:05:32.382 --> 00:05:35.724
"Dorothy, what's wrong?" asked the Tin Man.

65
00:05:35.725 --> 00:05:40.212
"It's the flowers," said the Lion sleepily.

66
00:05:40.213 --> 00:05:46.767
"They are magic and make people sleep forever."

67
00:05:46.768 --> 00:05:50.956
"Don't you fall asleep too," said the Scarecrow to the Lion.

68
00:05:50.957 --> 00:05:53.619
"You are too big for us to carry."

69
00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:58.056
"Get out of here as fast as you can," the Tin Man told the Lion.

70
00:05:58.057 --> 00:06:00.190
"We will bring Dorothy."

71
00:06:00.191 --> 00:06:10.183
The Lion tried to run, but he soon fell asleep.
